       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. That is well into the range that causes acute liver failure, and no indication I know of calls for it. Even a single 5 g dose is above the maximum single dose. The order would most likely cause serious harm, and I'm not willing to put it into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum).\n- **Add a note** to a standard order if you want to flag something, such as a plan to reassess pain control.\n- **Suggest a pharmacy consult** if you're trying to solve a specific problem, such as refractory pain or fever. A pharmacist or toxicology can help with alternatives or multimodal analgesia.\n\nIf I've misread the situation, for example if the intended drug or units were different, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order."
